{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When You did.</b> The meaning: when You were doing." "<b>and be seen.</b> It is an attribute of the Name, in the manner of ועשיר יענה עזות (Proverbs 18:23)." "<b>[we did not hope].</b> We were not hoping to see their like." "<b>[You came down, etc.].b> And when You were coming down, then because of You the mountains flowed, and the meaning is that You have already done thus."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 64, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:54.414813930Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}